# partitor — split a score PDF (vector or scanned) into instrument part PDFs
#
# Engine commands: `pieces` lists the pieces in a PDF (title and page
# range). `detect` finds staves and systems on each page, gives every ink
# component one owner (a staff, the system header, or a known discard class),
# suggests the part of every staff, and writes a layout file plus an HTML
# preview. `build` repeats the analysis, checks it against the layout file,
# and writes one PDF per part. Ink is never split: each connected component
# goes whole to one owner. Ink is never lost silently: a staff that is not
# accepted, or discard outside the known classes, fails the run. The input
# PDF is never written.
#
# Library commands (DESIGN.md §2, §6) work on a library folder
# (PARTITOR_LIBRARY, default /var/lib/partitor/library): no command = menu; `new` takes a
# PDF from inbox/ into library/<id>-<slug>/ (<id>-source.pdf,
# <id>-score.yaml, <id>-proof.pdf, parts/NN-<part>-<piece>--<id>.pdf; id
# YYYY-MM-NNNN); list, show, set, expand, contract, rebuild. `rebuild ID
# [part ...]` builds only the parts / groups named (3, 2-4, Trombones); the
# other files in parts/ stay. --jobs N|auto (PARTITOR_JOBS): workers for the
# page analysis (detect, build) and the rendering (build) (auto: CPUs - 1, at most 6, within
# PARTITOR_MEMORY_MAX).
#
# Installed as lib/partitor-engine of the partitor folder, next to the package
# lib/partitor/. The code moves from this file into that package in small steps
# (docs/DESIGN.md §12); the names that moved are imported near the top of this file.
# Run it through /usr/local/sbin/partitor, which starts it as user partitor in a systemd
# sandbox. It refuses to run as root (PARTITOR_ALLOW_ROOT=1: tests only).
# Runs in the venv /opt/partitor/venv; label OCR uses tesseract.
#
# Usage:
#   partitor                               menu
#   partitor new [N] [--jobs N|auto] | list | show ID (review) | rebuild ID (build) | analyse ID
#   Edits are saved, not built (--build: build too):
#   partitor expand ID | contract ID | meta ID (title, composer, short composer)
#   partitor bars ID                       pickups, split bars, barlines, line
#                                          starts, letters; ? = help; v = proof
#   partitor proof ID                      draw proof.pdf again (bar numbers)
#   partitor parts ID                      parts: N=name, N=- (not extracted),
#                                          N=+, N+M (join N into M: two staves)
#   partitor groups ID                     group scores: Name=4,5,6
#   partitor set ID key=value ...          keys: see SET_KEYS (title, pages,
#                                          paper, gap, margin_side, ...)
#   partitor pieces SCORE.pdf
#   partitor detect SCORE.pdf [--pages A-B] [--parts "Canto,Alto,Tenore,Basso"]
#                   [--title T] [--subtitle S] [--composer C] [--dpi N]
#                   [--out DIR] [--page-header-sp SP] [--force] [--jobs N|auto]
#   partitor build  SCORE.pdf [--pages A-B] [--out DIR] [--paper a4|letter|ledger]
#                   [--scale F] [--gap SP] [--min-gap SP] [--clearance SP]
#                   [--page-count N] [--min-staff-mm MM] [--ink normal|darker]
#                   [--bar-numbers start|none] [--bar-raise SP] [--bar-size SP]
#                   [--margin-top MM] [--margin-bottom MM] [--margin-side MM]
#                   [--gutter MM] [--duplex auto|on|off] [--large on|off]
#                   [--reflow on|off] [--max-staff-mm MM] [--title-page auto|off]
#                   [--rests compress|keep] [--jobs N|auto]
#   partitor --sandbox-check [--library]   (installer self-test)
#
# ID: 12 = serial 12 of the current year, or 2026-10-0012 (old: 2026-012).
#
# Options:
#   --pages A-B
#       detect: analyse only source pages A to B (one piece of a
#       multi-work PDF; see `partitor pieces`). Stored in the layout file.
#       build: selects the same work directory (SCORE.pA-B.partitor/).
#   --parts LIST
#       Comma-separated part names, top staff first, for the fullest system.
#       A part on two staves (organ, continuo) is named twice. Without
#       --parts, names come from the printed staff labels (OCR).
#   --title / --subtitle / --composer TEXT
#       Title band text on page 1 of every part. Written to the layout.
#   --dpi N
#       Render resolution for analysis and output strips. Default 400.
#   --out DIR
#       Work directory. Default: SCORE.partitor/ next to the input
#       (SCORE.pA-B.partitor/ with --pages). Holds layout.yaml, preview/
#       and parts/.
#   --page-header-sp SP
#       Text above a page's first staff farther than SP staff spaces is
#       discarded (page title, running header). Default 6.0. Stored in
#       the layout file.
#   --force
#       Overwrite an existing layout file.
#   --paper a4|letter|ledger
#       Output paper size. Default from layout (letter). ledger = 17 x 11 in,
#       landscape: the lines can be 2.2 x as wide, so the staff reaches
#       --max-staff-mm; more pages. No large-print copy (it is 11x17).
#   --scale F
#       Largest staff size relative to the source. Default none: up to
#       --max-staff-mm, also limited by the page width.
#   --max-staff-mm MM
#       Largest staff height (top line to bottom line). Default 8.
#   --reflow on|off
#       EXPERIMENTAL, off by default, ON HOLD (0.3.0-dev.35): it does not
#       enlarge the single parts of Biber 2026-10-0003 (3.6-3.8 mm) or its
#       Trombones group (3.7 mm). For a larger staff use --paper ledger.
#       on: new lines, cut only at barlines, each continuation line with a
#       copy of the clef and key signature, so the staff can reach
#       --max-staff-mm when long source lines keep it small (more pages).
#       Lines that cannot be cut safely stay whole (the build says why).
#       A group is cut only at barlines that all its staves have; with
#       pages=auto its page budget is 1.5 x the pages without re-flow.
#       Default off; the library CLI offers it when the print is small
#       (staff under small_mm, 6.5).
#   --rests compress|keep
#       compress (default): a part whose staff in a system is empty (no
#       noteheads, no stems; only rests) is made a multi-bar rest, as when
#       the source leaves the staff out; a group score only when all its
#       staves are empty. Systems with a rehearsal mark, or ink that is not
#       a rest, stay as engraved (warned). keep: all staves as engraved.
#   --title-page auto|off
#       auto: a title page when the music fills 3+ pages printed
#       double-sided (the music then starts on a spread). Default auto.
#   --gap SP
#       Normal distance from one staff's bottom line to the next staff's
#       top line, in staff spaces. Default 10. The same for the whole part
#       (larger only where notes would collide).
#   --min-gap SP
#       Smallest gap used to save a page turn. Default 7.
#   --clearance SP
#       Minimum ink-to-ink distance between two lines. Default 1.0.
#   --page-count N
#       Fit each part on N pages. Default: fewest page turns (1-2 pages:
#       none, 3-4: one), then the largest staff, then the widest gap.
#   --min-staff-mm MM
#       Smallest staff height (top line to bottom line) used to save a
#       page turn. Default 5.0.
#   --bar-numbers start|none
#       Bar number at the start of each line (default) or none.
#   --bar-raise SP / --bar-size SP
#       Least bar number baseline height above the top line (default 1)
#       and its size (default 2); it also clears the clef by 0.5 sp.
#   --margin-top / --margin-bottom / --margin-side MM
#       Page margins (default 15 mm each; floor 5 mm).
#   --gutter MM / --duplex auto|on|off
#       Double-sided print: spine margin gutter mm wider than the outer
#       margin (default 5). auto = double-sided above 2 pages.
#   --large on|off
#       Also write a large-print copy of each part (default on): Letter ->
#       11x17 (page scaled to the 11 in width, at the top, crop marks at
#       the cut line), A4 -> A3. File <part>-11x17.pdf / <part>-A3.pdf.
#       Paper ledger: no copy (the sheet is 11x17 already).
#   --ink normal|darker
#       darker makes thin, light print bolder (1 px at 400 dpi).
#
# Exit codes:
#   0 — success
#   1 — failure (analysis, safety gate, unresolved '?' in layout, I/O)
#   2 — usage error
